  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Four kinds of delivery",
  "description": "Seven against seven with goalkeepers on about 55 × 45 metres. Cones mark a wide channel along both sidelines. Goals only count when they come straight from a delivery from a wide channel, or from a rebound or second ball that follows it.\n\nGo through four kinds of delivery before you start: low and hard to the near post, cut back towards the penalty spot, high to the far post, and in-swinging from the wing. The first goal from each kind is worth three points to the team; after that the same kind is worth one. A goal from a rebound or second ball is worth two. The coach keeps the score.\n\nVariation: all goals count, but goals from a delivery from a wide channel earn extra points. The diagram shows five outfield players per team and is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Look up before you deliver – where is the space, and who is heading for it?"
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "The attackers spread out: one to the near post, one to the far post and one who holds back for the cut-back."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "A cut-back works when the defenders are running towards their own goal."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Follow up every shot – rebounds and second balls count."
    }
  ],
